2026-11-19T17:38:12.0072335Z Run one block of tests/features.py, from a marker line to the next block.
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0072668Z 
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0073037Z     python3 tools/audit/seat/features_block.py [--prelude 'import line']... "<first line of the block>" [END]
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0073724Z     python3 tools/audit/seat/features_block.py [--prelude 'import line']... --through "<marker line>"
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0074395Z     python3 tools/audit/seat/features_block.py --emit-prelude OUT "<first line of the block>" [END]
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0074796Z 
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0075093Z features.py runs every block in one process, which takes tens of minutes on a
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0075738Z loaded seat; a mutation proof needs only the block that pins the mutated line.
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0076265Z The block is the text from the line containing START up to END (default: the
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0076775Z script's closing ``sys.exit``), executed in the namespace features.py's own
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0077320Z header builds -- ``R``, ``Coord``, the harness fakes -- with ``__file__``
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0077877Z pointing at features.py, so path arithmetic inside the block resolves as in
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0078456Z the full run. Exit status is the block's ``R.close``: 0 when every check passed.
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0079158Z Run from the repository root under the CI venv.
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0079397Z 
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0079673Z ``--prelude`` (repeatable) runs one line, typically an import an earlier block
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0080248Z made, before the block. ``--through MARKER`` takes no block: it runs the whole
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0080788Z script from the top up to the line holding MARKER, the state every earlier
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0081263Z block builds, and exits with that prefix's ``R.close``.
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0081596Z 
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0081915Z ``--emit-prelude OUT`` writes to OUT the earlier top-level statements the
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0082524Z block reads, found by running it until no ``NameError`` is left: each missing
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0083097Z name takes its last binding before the use (before the block, or before the
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0083633Z prelude statement that needed it at module level). Run the block with
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0084256Z ``--prelude 'exec(open("OUT").read())'``. It derives from the tree it runs on,
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0085119Z so a mutant run needs no hand-copied prelude; exits 0 once the block runs
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0085893Z without raising (its checks are not judged), 1 on a name no earlier statement
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0086603Z binds or on any other exception.
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0086845Z 
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0087439Z ``--self-test`` runs offline: it executes a two-check block it writes itself.
2026-11-19T17:38:12.0088152Z 
